Verified with --dry-run against a pristine `git archive HEAD` extraction.

1. utils.py - evo 1.38.0 made `max_diff` keyword-only in
   sync.associate_trajectories(); the value is unchanged (0.01), only the call form.
   Upstream pins an older evo, where the third positional argument was accepted.

2. loc_demo.py - mcl/vis_loc_result.py imports its sibling with a package-relative
   `from .visualizer import Visualizer`, so the repository-root loc_demo.py cannot
   import it as a top-level module; import it as a package module instead.

Separate from this patch, and involving no source change: the C++ particle-filter
extension must be built against a NumPy-2-aware pybind11. CMake's
find_package(pybind11) selects the distribution's pybind11 2.9.1
("/usr/lib/cmake/pybind11", reported as `Found pybind11: /usr/include (found
version "2.9.1")`), whose PyArrayDescr_Proxy hardcodes the NumPy 1.x descriptor
layout (`char flags; int type_num; int elsize; int alignment;`). NumPy 2.x uses
(`char _former_flags; int type_num; npy_uint64 flags; npy_intp elsize; ...`), so
`elsize` is read from the wrong offset, the dtype itemsize comes out as 0, and the
first numpy-to-C++ array conversion segfaults - on every rebuild. Build the
extension with the environment's own pybind11 (>= 2.12, which selects its
descriptor proxy from PyArray_RUNTIME_VERSION_) instead:

  cd mcl
  CMAKE_ARGS="-Dpybind11_DIR=$HOME/.venvs/ir-mcl/lib/python3.10/site-packages/pybind11/share/cmake/pybind11" \
    $HOME/.venvs/ir-mcl/bin/python -m pip install -e . --no-build-isolation

The environment used here keeps NumPy 2.2.6 and torch 2.14.1; no runtime dependency
was downgraded.

